---
import Entry from '../../../layouts/Entry.astro';
import UsCharityFinancialSearch from '../../../components/UsCharityFinancialSearch.astro';
import { url } from '../../../lib/site';
import manifest from '../../../../public/data/charity-financials/us/manifest.json';

const title = 'United States charity Form 990 finances';
const count = (value: number) => value.toLocaleString('en-US');
const sources = [{ title: 'Annual extract of tax-exempt organization financial data', publisher: 'Internal Revenue Service', url: manifest.sourcePage }];
---

<Entry title={title} eyebrow="The Record · Global Charity Index" summary="Search U.S. charity revenue, functional expenses and grant amounts in selected IRS Form 990 extracts." crumbs={[{label:'The Record',href:'/record/'},{label:'Global Charity Index',href:'/record/charity-index/'},{label:'Financial filings',href:'/record/charity-financials/'},{label:'United States'}]} sources={sources}>
  <p>This edition covers {count(manifest.counts.organizations)} EINs associated with {count(manifest.counts.includedPeriods)} dated Form 990 records. {count(manifest.counts.multiPeriod)} EINs have more than one period. The calendar years of filing are 2023 and 2024. The selected tax periods end in 2022, 2023 or 2024.</p>
  <UsCharityFinancialSearch />
  <p>Follow an example of grant-level reporting in the <a href={url('/record/funding-flows/iberia-hrsa/')}>Iberia health center’s federal award and audit records</a>.</p>
  <h2 id="coverage">Coverage and original data</h2>
  <p>The IRS publishes financial extracts by the year a return was filed. The month in each result is the end of the tax period. The extracts do not give the exact start or end day here. The IRS describes adjustments and transcription effects that can make an extract value differ from the original return.</p>
  <ul>{Object.entries(manifest.sources).map(([year, source]) => <li>
    <strong>Calendar-year {year} extract.</strong> {count(source.counts.selected)} selected records out of {count(source.counts.input)}.
    {' '}{count(source.counts.otherSubsection)} records carried another subsection code. {count(source.counts.outsidePeriod)} remaining records were outside the selected tax periods.
    {' '}<a href={source.archive}>Original ZIP</a> · <a href={source.documentation}>IRS field definitions</a>.
  </li>)}</ul>
  <p>The edition selects subsection 03 on full Form 990. The short-form and private-foundation extracts are separate editions. Form 990-N and organizations outside the filing scope require other sources. The edition includes historical EINs missing from the dated identity snapshot. {count(manifest.counts.registryMatches)} EINs matched that snapshot exactly. A missing match leaves current status unresolved.</p>
  <p>Amounts stay in U.S. dollars and retain published zeroes. Grant figures are broad expense categories and do not identify an individual recipient or place of delivery. Revenue, expenses and grant amounts can overlap across organizations, including transfers or related entities. Consult the original return and any consolidated statements to determine reporting scope.</p>
  <p>Public financial data are attributed to the Internal Revenue Service. Charitology selected and reformatted the fields. <a href={url('/data/charity-financials/us/manifest.json')} download="irs-form-990-financials-manifest.json">Download the coverage and source manifest</a> for the original fingerprints and all shard paths. Import EINs as text to preserve leading zeros.</p>
</Entry>
